You're the best!

250
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:38,780
Well, my skin is crawling.

251
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:42,905
But on the bright side, we turned
a powerful enemy into an ally.

252
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:46,940
That acar breeze is nice, you know?

253
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,940
Yeah, you got that right.

254
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:52,377
I had a funny feeling we'd be
the ones riding on the roof.

255
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:54,897
We're a skosh over capacity now,

256
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:58,392
so we had to strap a twin or
two to the roof of the wagon.

257
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:01,049
Well, Boxxo, you've
really outdone yourself.

258
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:05,937
I bet driving at a max speed through an
empty field would be quite exhilarating.

259
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:06,920
Hello there.

260
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:11,480
Boxxo, I'm sorry for what I did.

261
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,473
It's bad enough that I tried to use you,

262
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:18,168
but I also betrayed my friends
and the people of the dungeon.

263
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:23,120
I don't expect you to trust me again, but
I swear my backstabbing days are over.

264
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:28,120
I mean, my son is still a factor,
so maybe swear was the wrong word.

265
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:30,100
I trust you anyway.

266
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,697
That's what friends are for.

267
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:32,610
Good point.

268
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:36,737
I suppose if Master Boxo has faith
in you, I will too. We're good.

269
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:40,277
He has no reason to betray us so
long as Sulream is on our side.

270
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,480
I trust him, despite everything.

271
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:43,870
Huh.

272
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:45,837
Lamas and Co are ready
to forgive and forget.

273
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:50,320
But things are a little more
complicated for the former fools.

274
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,150
Evie?

275
00:15:52,233 --> 00:15:53,760
Shwee? Pity?

276
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:57,840
I'm sorry for abandoning
and betraying all of you.

277
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:00,200
I don't deserve forgiveness.

278
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:03,017
I know it won't help,
but I'm sorry as well.

279
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:04,340
Same goes for me!

280
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:06,080
I'm sorry too!

281
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:09,480
I am also very sorry!

282
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:11,982
You're misreading the situation.

283
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:15,829
That isn't the reason we're
still upset with you whatsoever.

284
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:20,278
Shui, it appears you'll have
to spell it out for him.

285
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:23,297
Are you too dense to
figure out why we're upset?

286
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:26,477
It hurts that you didn't trust
us enough to confide in us!

287
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,977
If we'd known what you were planning,

288
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:30,337
we would have tried our
hardest to talk you out of it!

289
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:33,817
If it had been a half-decent plan, we
would have been right there with you!

290
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:37,312
Instead, you chose to keep it
all inside and push us away!

291
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:42,286
I have also encouraged Shui's wrath for
hiding things, like my love of footwear.

292
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:45,057
We are literally called
the Menagerie of Fools.

293
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:48,477
There's no reason to be coy about
our problems or shortcomings.

294
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,325
We deserve to know everything.

295
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:54,912
Although, perhaps we don't need every
detail about your amorous adventures.

296
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,725
I, for one, do need every detail
about those amorous adventures.

297
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,280
What do you know?

298
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:05,596
Marksa must have dispensed
a sense of humor for Heavy.

299
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:12,760
So, anyway, in short, Heavy,
Swee, and Petty, thank you.

300
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:17,217
We're grateful that you still
care enough to get mad at us.

301
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:18,600
It really means a lot.

302
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:20,940
What about pity?

303
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:24,632
When I asked for advice,
everyone just got loud and angry.

304
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,660
Darling, we're not done.

305
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:29,234
Tell me about those amorous adventures.

306
00:17:29,420 --> 00:17:33,244
So ended the dramatic plot twist
with a whole menagerie of fools.

307
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:36,377
No one's saying there are
no sore feelings left,

308
00:17:36,460 --> 00:17:40,754
but at least the Cap and his fools
are back on the right side of history.

309
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:46,617
Several days later, Captain Kerioyl and
his fam were already on their feet again.

310
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:48,759
They even started training with us.

311
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:53,760
As for the Ice Lady, she's
sticking to Kai like superglue.

312
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:57,861
Not exactly being chatty, but at
least she's not trying to kill us.

313
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,157
There's no need to be on
your guard, Magic Box.

314
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,337
I have no intention of
launching an attack.

315
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:06,361
I no longer serve the Demon Lord.

316
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,286
As such, I cannot afford
to make more enemies.

317
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:15,748
No matter what happens, I pick you swear
I'll always be on your side, big sis.

318
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,180
You're so precious to me.

319
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:19,773
You're all that I need.

320
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,241
That's one way to turn a villain.

321
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,852
It's pretty clear she'd never betray him.

322
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:29,220
Our journey's going smoothly, I think.

323
00:18:31,020 --> 00:18:33,720
There are no monsters or roadblocks.

324
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:36,260
Just us and the long, straight road.

325
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:08,057
This cruise could have used some
blue skies and green fields,

326
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:10,720
But it's total darkness,

327
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:14,491
other than the headlights and
the warm glow of magic items.

328
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:42,820
There's an end, isn't there?

329
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:45,200
I mean, there's gotta be, right?

330
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:14,000
Look, up ahead!

331
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:17,960
Am I dreaming or is that a wall?

332
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,717
I was starting to think
we'd never make it.

333
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:37,680
Shame here.

334
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:40,586
Looks like the middle
path was the right idea.

335
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:44,317
There's no way to know if this really
means we've reached the Inner Depths.

336
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:45,518
Eddie's devastated.

337
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:48,782
I wanted to travel a whole
lot longer with Boxxo.

338
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:52,540
If we encounter any foes,
worry not. I'll take them.

339
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,940
What kind of weirdness awaits?

340
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:58,108
Alright, I'm gonna try
to manhandle it open.

341
00:20:58,280 --> 00:21:01,520
I'm not seeing any traps,
but please be cautious. Hmm.

342
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:24,217
I'm trying my best to make it open,
but the thing isn't even budging.

343
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:26,500
If Llamas' strength isn't enough,

344
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:30,622
perhaps there's some special step
we must take to unlock it first.

345
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:34,977
That shape, it makes me think
there's something that goes in there.

346
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:37,097
We gave the doors the once over.

347
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:39,257
But the only things that stood out.

348
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,869
Were those wacky cavities.

349
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:43,217
There's just gotta be something.

350
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:46,080
That perfectly matches
that size and shape.

351
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:49,720
Insert coins.

352
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,120
The stratum lord coins.

353
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,697
I've got a hot hunch brewing.

354
00:21:58,780 --> 00:22:00,437
And it's screaming at me.

355
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,080
This is what those stratum coins are for.

356
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,637
It's too big and hot.

357
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,817
I'm gonna be a little more.

358
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:12,297
I'm gonna be so busy.

359
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:14,700
I'm gonna be a new story.

360
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,037
I'll be a new story.

361
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:25,717
I can't wait. I can't wait.

362
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:26,630
I can't wait.

363
00:22:26,713 --> 00:22:27,840
I can't wait.

364
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,260
Oh?

365
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:17,637
Thank you so

366
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:23,177
much for

367
00:23:23,260 --> 00:23:27,420
watching.

368
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:37,840
I look forward to serving you again.
